PROPOSED CHANGE OUTSIDE THIS BRIEF'S WRITE LIST -- NOT APPLIED. (pri 126)

TARGET  experiments/exp_board_rows_on_the_reader_v1.py  (pri 122's landed cell -- the fixed scorer this
        instrument imports; a solver may not edit it, so it is proposed here as a diff.)

WHAT IS WRONG, WITH THE NUMBER THAT FOUND IT.  The `state` row's information-free TWIN shuffles the gold
holders WITHIN ONE SENTENCE (`holders = [h for (h, p, ty) in gold_states]; rng.shuffle(shuf)`).  A sentence
with a single predicational clause -- the common case -- therefore hands the holder back to itself and the
twin IS the model.  Measured on the sealed modern holdout (279 documents, 139 state items): model 0.7410,
twin 0.6906, model - twin +0.0504 [+0.0142,+0.0981].  Only about 5% of items ever received a different
holder, so the state row's "the twin loses" check is close to vacuous.  It is NOT a property of short
documents: the chunk-matched arm (8 sealed documents concatenated, identical token stream) reproduces the
twin at 0.6906 exactly, because the shuffle is sentence-scoped, not unit-scoped.

THE FIX.  Collect the unit's state items during the sentence loop and score the twin AFTER it, permuting the
holders ACROSS the whole scoring unit (with a derangement attempt so a holder is not handed back to itself).
The `model` and `most_recent_noun` arms are untouched, item-for-item, so no published model or floor number
moves; only the twin becomes genuinely information-free.

RISK OF THIS RECOMMENDATION, STATED.  It will LOWER the published state twin and therefore WIDEN the
state model-minus-twin margin on every population, sealed and read.  That is a number moving in the
flattering direction because a control was made stricter, and it must be reported that way, not as a gain.
It also changes `state` twin numbers in every historical landing record, so the board's state twin column is
not comparable across the change and the landing record should carry a scorer-version marker.

NOT VERIFIED BY A RUN.  The patched copy parses and the edit is mechanical, but it has NOT been executed:
running it would require the strategy session to land it in hdlab/experiments and re-run the board.

